  "term": "yin and yang",
  "definition": "Yin and yang is a Chinese philosophical idea that describes reality as arising from the interaction of two opposite yet connected forces, such as dark and light, feminine and masculine, or cold and hot. In this view, health depends on a balanced relationship between these paired qualities, and imbalance is linked with illness.",
